{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"You do not want secrets, git metadata, or install trees in durable storage. The\ndefault snapshot policy excludes those paths. When a capture or restore finds\nan unsafe filesystem entry, it stops."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Portable snapshots store regular files and directories only. When a capture or\nrestore finds a symlink, an executable file, or a special filesystem entry, it\nfails with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"SandboxSnapshotError"},{"type":"text","value":" code\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"SANDBOX_SNAPSHOT_UNSUPPORTED_ENTRY"},{"type":"text","value":". Exclude scripts, hooks, and other\nexecutable files in "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"policy.exclude"},{"type":"text","value":". An executable bit on a regular file\nstops the whole capture or restore."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"default-exclusions","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Default exclusions"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The default policy excludes these path segments at every depth:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":".git"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"node_modules"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":".env*"}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"It also excludes these exact paths:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The projection marker, "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":".tanstack-projected-<workspaceHash>"},{"type":"text","value":", at the\nworkspace root only."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"CLAUDE.md"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"GEMINI.md"},{"type":"text","value":" at the workspace root."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Direct "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":".claude/skills/<name>"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":".codex/skills/<name>"},{"type":"text","value":", and\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":".grok/skills/<name>"},{"type":"text","value":" paths."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"These exclusions use paths for regular files and copied files too."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"replace-the-default-policy","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Replace the default policy"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"To keep only some files, or one file, see\n"},{"type":"link","href":"./portable-snapshots-files","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Pick Which Files to Keep"}]},{"type":"text","value":". If you pass only\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"include"},{"type":"text","value":" or only "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"redact"},{"type":"text","value":", the default exclusions stay in place. If you\npass "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"exclude"},{"type":"text","value":", copy "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"defaultSandboxSnapshotPolicy()"},{"type":"text","value":" first. Then add your\nrules."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { defaultSandboxSnapshotPolicy } from '@tanstack/ai-sandbox'\n\nconst policy = {\n  ...defaultSandboxSnapshotPolicy(),\n  redact({ bytes }: { bytes: Uint8Array }) {\n    return bytes\n  },\n}","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"When you create the snapshots object, pass "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"policy"},{"type":"text","value":". See\n"},{"type":"link","href":"./portable-snapshots-configure","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Keep Files After Reload"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The exact projection marker for the workspace stays protected. A custom policy\ncannot capture or restore that marker."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"secrets","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Secrets"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Resolved secret values are replaced with zero bytes before the content is\nhashed or stored."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"restore-safety","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Restore safety"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"An invalid manifest, a missing blob, or changed blob content stops the restore\nbefore it writes the workspace. The failed private sandbox is then discarded.\nYour existing resumed sandbox stays unchanged."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"See "},{"type":"link","href":"./providers","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Providers"}]},{"type":"text","value":" for provider-native snapshot and resume support."}]}],"headings":[{"id":"default-exclusions","text":"Default exclusions","level":2},{"id":"replace-the-default-policy","text":"Replace the default policy","level":2},{"id":"secrets","text":"Secrets","level":2},{"id":"restore-safety","text":"Restore safety","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\nYou do not want secrets, git metadata, or install trees in durable storage. The\ndefault snapshot policy excludes those paths. When a capture or restore finds\nan unsafe filesystem entry, it stops.\n\nPortable snapshots store regular files and directories only. When a capture or\nrestore finds a symlink, an executable file, or a special filesystem entry, it\nfails with `SandboxSnapshotError` code\n`SANDBOX_SNAPSHOT_UNSUPPORTED_ENTRY`. Exclude scripts, hooks, and other\nexecutable files in `policy.exclude`. An executable bit on a regular file\nstops the whole capture or restore.\n\n## Default exclusions\n\nThe default policy excludes these path segments at every depth:\n\n- `.git`\n- `node_modules`\n- `.env*`\n\nIt also excludes these exact paths:\n\n- The projection marker, `.tanstack-projected-<workspaceHash>`, at the\n  workspace root only.\n- `CLAUDE.md` and `GEMINI.md` at the workspace root.\n- Direct `.claude/skills/<name>`, `.codex/skills/<name>`, and\n  `.grok/skills/<name>` paths.\n\nThese exclusions use paths for regular files and copied files too.\n\n## Replace the default policy\n\nTo keep only some files, or one file, see\n[Pick Which Files to Keep](./portable-snapshots-files). If you pass only\n`include` or only `redact`, the default exclusions stay in place. If you\npass `exclude`, copy `defaultSandboxSnapshotPolicy()` first. Then add your\nrules.\n\n```ts\nimport { defaultSandboxSnapshotPolicy } from '@tanstack/ai-sandbox'\n\nconst policy = {\n  ...defaultSandboxSnapshotPolicy(),\n  redact({ bytes }: { bytes: Uint8Array }) {\n    return bytes\n  },\n}\n```\n\nWhen you create the snapshots object, pass `policy`. See\n[Keep Files After Reload](./portable-snapshots-configure).\n\nThe exact projection marker for the workspace stays protected. A custom policy\ncannot capture or restore that marker.\n\n## Secrets\n\nResolved secret values are replaced with zero bytes before the content is\nhashed or stored.\n\n## Restore safety\n\nAn invalid manifest, a missing blob, or changed blob content stops the restore\nbefore it writes the workspace. The failed private sandbox is then discarded.\nYour existing resumed sandbox stays unchanged.\n\nSee [Providers](./providers) for provider-native snapshot and resume support.\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\ntitle: What a Snapshot Stores\nid: portable-snapshots-safety\norder: 16\ndescription: \"See which workspace paths a portable snapshot stores, and how capture treats secrets and unsafe files.\"\n---\n\nYou do not want secrets, git metadata, or install trees in durable storage. The\ndefault snapshot policy excludes those paths. When a capture or restore finds\nan unsafe filesystem entry, it stops.\n\nPortable snapshots store regular files and directories only. When a capture or\nrestore finds a symlink, an executable file, or a special filesystem entry, it\nfails with `SandboxSnapshotError` code\n`SANDBOX_SNAPSHOT_UNSUPPORTED_ENTRY`. Exclude scripts, hooks, and other\nexecutable files in `policy.exclude`. An executable bit on a regular file\nstops the whole capture or restore.\n\n## Default exclusions\n\nThe default policy excludes these path segments at every depth:\n\n- `.git`\n- `node_modules`\n- `.env*`\n\nIt also excludes these exact paths:\n\n- The projection marker, `.tanstack-projected-<workspaceHash>`, at the\n  workspace root only.\n- `CLAUDE.md` and `GEMINI.md` at the workspace root.\n- Direct `.claude/skills/<name>`, `.codex/skills/<name>`, and\n  `.grok/skills/<name>` paths.\n\nThese exclusions use paths for regular files and copied files too.\n\n## Replace the default policy\n\nTo keep only some files, or one file, see\n[Pick Which Files to Keep](./portable-snapshots-files). If you pass only\n`include` or only `redact`, the default exclusions stay in place. If you\npass `exclude`, copy `defaultSandboxSnapshotPolicy()` first. Then add your\nrules.\n\n```ts\nimport { defaultSandboxSnapshotPolicy } from '@tanstack/ai-sandbox'\n\nconst policy = {\n  ...defaultSandboxSnapshotPolicy(),\n  redact({ bytes }: { bytes: Uint8Array }) {\n    return bytes\n  },\n}\n```\n\nWhen you create the snapshots object, pass `policy`. See\n[Keep Files After Reload](./portable-snapshots-configure).\n\nThe exact projection marker for the workspace stays protected. A custom policy\ncannot capture or restore that marker.\n\n## Secrets\n\nResolved secret values are replaced with zero bytes before the content is\nhashed or stored.\n\n## Restore safety\n\nAn invalid manifest, a missing blob, or changed blob content stops the restore\nbefore it writes the workspace. The failed private sandbox is then discarded.\nYour existing resumed sandbox stays unchanged.\n\nSee [Providers](./providers) for provider-native snapshot and resume support.\n"}
